# makefile.include.nvhpc_acc.changes
# =============================================================================
# This is NOT a makefile and NOT a copy of the official template.
# It lists the edits applied on top of the OpenACC GPU templates shipped with
# VASP 6.6.x:
#   arch/makefile.include.nvhpc_acc                 (NVHPC libs + FFTW)
#   arch/makefile.include.nvhpc_omp_acc             (+ OpenMP)
#   arch/makefile.include.nvhpc_ompi_mkl_omp_acc    (+ OpenMP, MKL on the CPU
#                                                    side; recommended on
#                                                    Intel host CPUs)
#
# Workflow:
#   module load nvhpc/25.1            # site specific; NVHPC >= 21.2,
#                                     # avoid 22.1 and 22.2 (OpenMP bug)
#   cp arch/makefile.include.nvhpc_acc makefile.include
#   # apply items A-F, then
#   make veryclean && make DEPS=1 -j 16 all
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A. GPU architecture and CUDA version
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wherever the template passes "-gpu=..." to the compilers (CC/FC/FCL lines
# or a helper variable, depending on the release), adapt:
#   compute capability : V100 -> cc70, A100/A30 -> cc80, L4/L40 -> cc89,
#                         H100/H200 -> cc90, or ccnative when compiling on
#                         the GPU node itself. Several values (cc80,cc90)
#                         give a portable but slower-to-build binary.
#   CUDA version        : must match a CUDA shipped with your NVHPC
#                         (check: ls $NVHPC_ROOT/cuda/ or nvcc --version)

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B. NVROOT and the QD library (quadruple precision emulation)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The template derives NVROOT from the location of nvfortran. If that fails,
# set it by hand, e.g.
#   NVROOT = /opt/nvidia/hpc_sdk/Linux_x86_64/25.1
# At run time the QD library must be found:
#   export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$NVROOT/compilers/extras/qd/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C. CPU-side FFT / BLAS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# nvhpc_acc / nvhpc_omp_acc : BLAS, LAPACK, ScaLAPACK come with NVHPC,
#                             FFTW must be installed by you:
#   FFTW_ROOT ?= $(HOME)/opt/fftw-3.3.10-nvhpc
# nvhpc_ompi_mkl_omp_acc   : FFTW/BLAS/LAPACK/ScaLAPACK from MKL; make sure
#                             MKLROOT is set and export at run time
#                             MKL_THREADING_LAYER=INTEL

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D. Precompiler options
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep the defaults of the 6.6.x template (OpenACC code paths, NCCL, QD
# emulation, ...). Since VASP 6.5.0 OpenACC is activated by -DACC_OFFLOAD
# together with -DNVCUDA; the old -D_OPENACC belongs to <= 6.4 templates.
# Never reuse a makefile.include from an older VASP release.
# Do NOT add -Dlibbeef or -DUSELIBXC: not supported by the GPU ports.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# E. HDF5 (append to the end of makefile.include)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HDF5 must be compiled with nvfortran/nvc (Fortran .mod files are
# compiler specific):
#   CC=nvc FC=nvfortran ./configure --prefix=$HOME/opt/hdf5-1.14.5-nvhpc --enable-fortran
CPP_OPTIONS += -DVASP_HDF5
HDF5_ROOT   ?= $(HOME)/opt/hdf5-1.14.5-nvhpc
LLIBS       += -L$(HDF5_ROOT)/lib -lhdf5_fortran -Wl,-rpath,$(HDF5_ROOT)/lib
INCS        += -I$(HDF5_ROOT)/include

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# F. Run-time rules for the GPU binary (put them into the job script)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   * exactly one MPI rank per GPU
#   * OMP_NUM_THREADS = free CPU cores per rank (needs an *_omp_* build)
#   * INCAR: KPAR = number of GPUs (if the irreducible k points divide
#     evenly), NSIM = 16-32; NCORE is reset to 1 automatically
#   * a CUDA-aware MPI is required (the OpenMPI bundled with NVHPC is)
